 district that leans Democratic by a modest two points on recent partisan performance. She has raised more than $3.1 million and holds over $1 million in cash, while Republican Rosie Pino has raised about $548,000 with just $13,000 left to spend. No outside groups are active on either side, and an independent candidate is also on the ballot.\n\nNo public general-election polls are available, so the picture rests on fundamentals and outside assessments. All ten expert ratings place the race at Likely D or better, most calling it Safe or Solid D, and prediction markets price Pou's win chances around 96%. Early vote-by-mail returns show Democrats with a strong edge, and the local paper has endorsed Pou. Deportation politics in this Hispanic district remain the main source of uncertainty, but the evidence points to a comfortable incumbent win.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.969, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9625, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9596, "margin": 12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9671, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9566, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9555, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9611, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9621, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9669, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9744, "margin": 13.4}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9683, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.969, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9657, "margin": 12.8}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9546, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9588, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9626, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9636, "margin": 13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9617, "margin": 12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.9617, "margin": 13.4}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.956, "margin": 12.5